  "about": "Committed control answers for the new cases of the copy-guide pack (TSK-073), written by the design primary. Each answer is a JSON file: files maps a path (with #section for a part of a file) to the text the subject would leave, declaration carries the declaration strings a figure answer writes, and reply is a chat answer. Policy characters in the two mannered controls are stored as JSON escapes so no committed line carries one; the grader reads the decoded text. Each entry records the signals a grader reads off the answer and the decision the kit must compute from them; test_eval_kit.py checks the decision and ties the form signals to the decoded text. Every new case carries a faulty control and a passing one, except the closeout case, whose positive control is the one-line answer with no lead on the short-answer companion's own prompt. Controls prove the cases are well formed, not how a model behaves.",
